   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Hidden cities is a joint WHO / UN-HABITAT report about urbanization and global health issues. Photo stories from around the world reflect the hidden realities urban dwellers are facing, and highlight some health inequities.&#xA;&#xA;A woman uses a home made device, a small plastic container attached to a stick, to remove garbage from the water in front of her home. Isla Putting Bato, a shanty area built on top of a breakwater. It now has many permanent cement houses. Manila, Philippines.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:rights>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Â© WHO / Anna Kari</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
