     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Fauzan Ijazah</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The waste management operator performs septage at the community sewerage system in Candimulyo Village, Temanggung District, Central Java Province, Indonesia.&#xA;&#xA;Community Sewerage System is built through State Budget funded SANIMAS Program implemented by the Ministry of Public Works and Housing (MPWH) in Candimulyo Village, Temanggung District. The sewerage system is connected to houses using pipes, and equipped with public space that can be utilized for community activities or gathering. The communal sanitation system is managed by KSM Jadi Bersih, a community self-help group.  &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;SANIMAS (Sanitasi oleh Masyarakat or Sanitation by Communities) is the governmenr program of decentralized community managed wastewater system which may include public facilities or decentralized sewarage system with communal treatment facilities. The MPWH developed a community-led approach to installing communal sanitation system that serves 50-100 households. In 2006, the concept was adopted and has been rapidly expanded by MPWH, local governments, donor agencies and NGOs. &#xA;&#xA;</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
